  "source_review": [
    "No native requirement for writer_enabled=false; disk capability refusal precedes output directory creation and queue/frame mutation.",
    "Session name is a safe leaf; final session directory is created exclusively; existing session refuses rather than overwriting retained files.",
    "Immutable new frame files are not overwritten; full post-close bytes gate each write and written_frames increments only after all three applicable frame files succeed.",
    "One writer thread owns disk output; immutable snapshots and existing mutex/semaphore lifecycle remain unchanged; no new access to mutable World, Rapier or live scene tree.",
    "Initial and final recording.json use the reviewed shared native replacement helper. Failure to replace leaves initial valid recording disposition and reports failed; no complete recording inferred from partial frame files.",
    "Shared utility only creates a RefCounted bridge and performs file replacement; the ordinary distribution supplies the native capability but historical GDScript-only hosts explicitly refuse disk recording."
  ],
  "review_requests_resolved": [
    "Added engine-error-log refusal even when process exits zero and expected result markers exist.",
    "Guide now describes Linux file-size fault and Windows locked-manifest runner separately."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Linux actual RLIMIT_FSIZE and normal recording executed independently here; Windows requires its own hosted receipt.",
    "A recording spans multiple files; it is not a transaction, exact replay, power-loss guarantee or hostile-concurrent-filesystem protection.",
    "Extra writer reads need inclusion in future matched owner recording OFF/ON performance evaluation; none claimed here."
  ]
